    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": 17449,
        "title": "Return Statement",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 148011,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A function can return a value to the code that called it. This mini game UI uses a function that returns a value to help update the score.</p><webview version=\"2\" content=\"&lt;!doctype html&gt;&#xA;&lt;html&gt;&#xA; &lt;head&gt;&#xA;  &lt;style&gt;&#xA;   body {&#xA;    text-align: center;&#xA;    font-size: 16px;&#xA;    margin: 0 auto;&#xA;    background-color: #D5F5E3&#xA;   }&#xA;   &#xA;   button {&#xA;    background-color: #85C1E9;&#xA;    border: none;&#xA;    border-radius: 8px;&#xA;    color: white;&#xA;    text-align: center;&#xA;    text-decoration: none;&#xA;    display: inline-block;&#xA;    font-size: 14px;&#xA;    padding: 6px 12px;&#xA;    margin: 0 12px 0 0;&#xA;   }&#xA;   &#xA;   h2 {&#xA;    color: #7c795d;&#xA;    font-family: 'Trocchi', serif;&#xA;    font-size: 45px;&#xA;    font-weight: normal;&#xA;    line-height: 48px;&#xA;    margin: 0;&#xA;    text-align: centre&#xA;   }&#xA;   &#xA;   #hud {&#xA;    text-align: left;&#xA;    max-width: 420px;&#xA;    margin: 0 auto;&#xA;   }&#xA;  &lt;/style&gt;&#xA; &lt;/head&gt;&#xA; &lt;body id=&quot;main&quot;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h2&gt;Score Booster&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Add points for collecting a coin.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div id=&quot;hud&quot;&gt;&#xA;   &lt;p&gt;&#xA;    &lt;label&gt;Coins Collected&lt;/label&gt;&#xA;    &lt;input id=&quot;inputCoins&quot; type=&quot;number&quot; placeholder=&quot;Coins&quot;&gt;&#xA;   &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;   &lt;button onClick=&quot;updateScore()&quot;&gt;add to score&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;   &lt;p&gt;Score: &lt;span id=&quot;outputScore&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;script&gt;&#xA;   function pointsFromCoins(coins) {&#xA;    return coins * 100;&#xA;   }&#xA;   function updateScore() {&#xA;    const coins = Number(document.getElementById(&quot;inputCoins&quot;).value);&#xA;    document.getElementById(&quot;outputScore&quot;).innerHTML = pointsFromCoins(coins);&#xA;   }&#xA;  &lt;/script&gt;&#xA; &lt;/body&gt;&#xA;&lt;/html&gt;\" /></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 148012,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To return something from a function we add the <code>return</code> keyword followed by the value to return, like here with <code>return status;</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option startIndex=\"72\" endIndex=\"78\" /><option startIndex=\"78\" endIndex=\"79\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"playerStatus\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"hp\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" status = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Player HP: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + hp;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" status;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return</code>, followed by <code>status</code>, and finally <code>;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 148013,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A function can return any type of value, like a string, number, or boolean. This function returns the number value inside <code>damage</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"74\" endIndex=\"80\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"critDamage\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"baseDamage\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" damage = baseDamage * \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" damage;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>damage</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 148014,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can only return a single value. Here, we return the boolean value inside the variable with <code>return isAlive;</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"55\" endIndex=\"61\" /><option startIndex=\"62\" endIndex=\"69\" /><option startIndex=\"69\" endIndex=\"70\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"isPlayerAlive\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"hp\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" isAlive = hp &gt; \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" isAlive;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return</code>, followed by <code>isAlive</code>, and finally <code>;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 148015,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can use the return value of a function like any value by calling the function. Here, we call <code>playerStatus(22)</code> to use its value.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"94\" endIndex=\"106\" /><option startIndex=\"106\" endIndex=\"107\" /><option startIndex=\"107\" endIndex=\"109\" /><option startIndex=\"109\" endIndex=\"110\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"playerStatus\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"hp\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" status = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Player HP: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + hp;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" status;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerStatus(\" /><text value=\"22\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"));\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>playerStatus</code> followed by <code>(</code> and then <code>22</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 148016,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can store the return value in a variable too. Here we store the return value in <code>result</code> and display it in the console.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"88\" endIndex=\"94\" /><option startIndex=\"115\" endIndex=\"122\" /><option startIndex=\"122\" endIndex=\"123\" /><option startIndex=\"123\" endIndex=\"126\" /><option startIndex=\"127\" endIndex=\"133\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"playerStatus\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"hp\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" status = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Player HP: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + hp;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" status;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" result = playerStatus(\" /><text value=\"29\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(result);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>result</code> followed by <code>console</code> and then <code>.</code>, <code>log</code>, <code>result</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 148017,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>If we don't include a <code>return</code> statement, the function returns the value <code>undefined</code> instead.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"111\" endIndex=\"117\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"playerStatus\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"hp\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" status = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Player HP: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + hp;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" result = playerStatus(\" /><text value=\"29\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(result);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>result</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 148018,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How do we return a value from a function?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">By adding the return keyword followed by the value to return</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">By adding the value and then the return keyword on the next line</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">By adding the return keyword followed by the value to return.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 148019,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which type of value can a function return?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A function can return any type of value, like a string, number or boolean</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A function can only return strings and numbers</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A function can return any type of value, like a string, number or boolean.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 148020,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the number of values a function can return?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A function can return a single value</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Functions can return multiple values</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A function can return a single value.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 148021,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How do we use the return value of a function?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">We call the function and use it like any other value</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">We don't call the function if we want to use the return value</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">We call the function and use it like any other value.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 148022,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How do we store the return value in a variable?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">We call the function and store it in a variable </item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">We add the variable to the end of the function</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">We call the function and store it in a variable .</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 148023,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What happens when we don't include the <code>return</code> statement in our function?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The function returns the value <code>undefined</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">There's an infinite loop in the function</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The function returns the value <code>undefined</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #14",
            "id": 148024,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Return the value from this function.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"number\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"24\" endIndex=\"30\" /><option startIndex=\"31\" endIndex=\"33\" /><option startIndex=\"33\" endIndex=\"34\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"giveMeTen\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(giveMeTen());\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return</code>, followed by <code>10</code>, and finally <code>;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #15",
            "id": 148025,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Return the string by coding <code>message;</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"81\" endIndex=\"89\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"lootMessage\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"item\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" message = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Loot collected: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + item;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" message;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" result = lootMessage(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Health Potion&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(result);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>message;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #16",
            "id": 148026,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Return a single value from this function.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"var\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"62\" /><option startIndex=\"63\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option startIndex=\"72\" endIndex=\"73\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"hasLowHealth\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"hp\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" lowHealth = hp &lt; \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" lowHealth;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" result = hasLowHealth(\" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(result);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return</code>, followed by <code>lowHealth</code>, and finally <code>;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #17",
            "id": 148027,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Call the <code>addTen()</code> function with a value.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"89\" endIndex=\"95\" /><option startIndex=\"95\" endIndex=\"96\" /><option startIndex=\"96\" endIndex=\"98\" /><option startIndex=\"98\" endIndex=\"99\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"addTen\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"number\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" addedTen = \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" + number;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" addedTen;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(addTen(\" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"));\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>addTen</code> followed by <code>(</code> and then <code>20</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #18",
            "id": 148028,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create the <code>result</code> variable and store the return value of the function inside.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"95\" endIndex=\"100\" /><option startIndex=\"101\" endIndex=\"107\" /><option startIndex=\"121\" endIndex=\"130\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"startLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"player\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" status = player + \" /><text value=\"&quot; entered the level&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" status;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" result = startLevel(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Desmond&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>const</code>, followed by <code>result</code>, and finally <code>\"Desmond\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #19",
            "id": 148029,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Display <code>undefined</code> in the console, by calling the <code>gameOver()</code> function with the value <code>\"Ann\"</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"86\" endIndex=\"102\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"gameOver\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"player\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" message = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Game Over: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\" + player;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" result = gameOver(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Ann&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(result);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>gameOver(\"Ann\");</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}